$
$ Database for high Mn steels (Fe-Mn-Al-Si-V-Nb-Ti-C-N), Ver. 4.0
$
$ Compiled by Bengt Hallstedt, March 2014 (first version November 2010,
$ second version December 2012, third version February 2014)
$
$ ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$
$ Version information
$ ===================
$
$ Changes from version 3.0 to 4.0:
$
$ Ti is added to the database. This includes the systems Fe-Ti, Ti-C, Ti-N,
$ Mn-Ti, Al-Ti, Si-Ti, Nb-Ti, Ti-V, Fe-Ti-C, Fe-Ti-N, Ti-C-N, Nb-Ti-C,
$ Nb-Ti-N, Ti-V-C and Ti-V-N.
$
$ Changes from version 2.1 to 3.0:
$
$ Al-Fe-Mn: Updated from Umino 2006 to Lindahl 2013.
$ Fe-Nb-V:  Added from Khvan 2013.
$
$ Changes from version 1.0 to 2.1:
$
$ The Al-Fe-Mn-C system is still very much in work, but some more recent data
$ have been added.
$
$ Al-Fe: Updated from Seierstein 1993 to Sundman 2009.
$        The phase BCC_4SL was added (4SL-BCC). The disordered part is
$        A2_BCC (as for BCC_2SL, which remains).
$        The phase AL5FE4 was replaced by AL8FE5_D82.
$ Al-Mn: Updated from Jansson 1998 to Du 2007 with ordering modelling added
$        for fcc and bcc and modification of fcc and Al11Mn4_HT
$        by Djurovic 2011.
$        The phases AL4MN_LAMBDA and AL11MN4_HT were added.
$        The model of AL8MN5_D810 was changed from 12:4:10 to 12:5:9.
$ Fe-C:  Cementite modified.
$ Fe-Mn: HCP_A3 interaction slightly modified.
$ Fe-N:  Updated from Frisk 1991 to Du 1993.
$ Fe-Nb: Updated from Lee 2001 to Liu 2012/Khvan 2013
$ Mn-C:  Updated from Huang 1990 to Djurovic 2010.
$ Mn-Nb: Added from Liu 2012.
$ Nb-C:  Slight change of BCC_A2 (Khvan 2013).
$ Nb-N:  BCC_A2 reoptimised (Khvan 2013).
$ V-C:   Liquid interaction slightly modified.
$ Al-Fe-Mn: Updated from Jansson 1998 to Umino 2006. However, Umino used
$           older versions of Al-Fe and Al-Mn than included here, so more
$           work will be necessary.
$ Fe-C-N:   Updated from Du 1991 to Du 1993.
$ Fe-Mn-Nb: Added from Liu 2012/Khvan 2013.
$ Fe-Nb-C:  Updated from Lee 2001 to Khvan 2013.
$ Fe-Nb-N:  Updated from Lee 2001 to Khvan 2013.
$ Mn-Nb-C:  Added from Khvan 2012.
$ Mn-Nb-N:  Added from Khvan 2013.
$ Nb-C-N:   Updated from Lee 2001 to Khvan 2013.
$ Fe-Mn-Nb-C:  Added from Khvan 2012.
$ Fe-Mn-Nb-N:  Added from Khvan 2013.
$
 DATABASE_INFO '
 Welcome to version 4.0 of the PrecHiMn database for cubic V(C,N) and'
 Nb(C,N) carbides and carbonitrides in high-Mn steels.''
 Created by Bengt Hallstedt in November 2010 and updated in December 2012'
 and February and March 2014.''
 The database contains the elements Fe, Mn, Al, Si, V, Nb, Ti, C and N.'''
 A few notes on phases in the database:''
 FCC_A1 is both austenite and cubic (Nb,Ti,V)(C,N). Thermo-Calc version S'
 will create the necessary composition sets automatically. With older'
 versions of Thermo-Calc this must be done manually in most cases.''
 HCP_A3 is both the epsilon-phase (epsilon-martensite) and the M2X'
 hexagonal carbide/nitride.''
 At high contents of Al or Si the BCC_A2 phase (ferrite) may order.'
 This is described by the BCC_2SL phase, which is deactivated by default.'
 To activate it, the following commands are needed in the database module:'
    RESTORE PHASE A2_BCC BCC_2SL'
    REJECT PHASE BCC_A2'
 All equilibria with BCC_A2 will be reproduced as before, but the phase'
 name will now be BCC_2SL.''
 CBCC_A12 is alpha-Mn and CUB_A13 is beta-Mn.''
 If you suspend the GRAPHITE to calculate equilibria with CEMENTITE,'
 you should also suspend DIAMOND. Otherwise DIAMOND may become more stable'
 than CEMENTITE at low temperature.''
 The GAS phase is deactivated by default, so if you need it activate it'
 in the database module:
    RESTORE PHASE GAS''
 The database contains quite a large number of phases that will be of'
 little interest in most cases. For calculations with several elements'
 it is recommended to suspend all phases except those actually needed'
 in order to speed up the calculations.'''
 All binary systems are included in the database. The ternary systems'
 Fe-Mn-C, Al-Fe-C, Fe-Si-C, Fe-V-C, Fe-Nb-C, Fe-Ti-C, Fe-C-N, Al-Fe-Mn,'
 Fe-Mn-Si, Fe-Mn-V, Fe-Mn-Nb, Fe-Mn-N, Al-Fe-N, Fe-V-N, Fe-Nb-N, Fe-Ti-N,'
 Al-Mn-C, Mn-V-C, Mn-Nb-C, Nb-V-C, Nb-Ti-C, Nb-Ti-N, Ti-V-C, Ti-V-N, V-C-N,
 Nb-C-N and Ti-C-N are included.''
 !
$
$ ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 TEMP-LIM 298.15 6000.00 !
$
$ELEMENT NAME  REF. STATE               ATOMIC MASS H298-H0    S298    !
$
 ELEMENT VA   VACUUM                      0.0          0.0      0.0    ! 
 ELEMENT NB   BCC_A2                     92.9064    5220.0     36.27   ! 
 ELEMENT TI   HCP_A3                     47.88      4824.      30.72   ! 
$ ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ Species
$
$ ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ Phase definitions
$
 PHASE LIQUID:L % 1 1 !
 CONST LIQUID:L : NB TI : !
$
$ Fcc (cF4, Fm-3m) and MeX (cF8, Fm-3m)
$

$
$ Bcc (cI2, Im-3m)
$
 PHASE BCC_A2 %B 1 1 !
 CONST BCC_A2 : NB% TI% : !

$ ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ Defaults
$
 FUNCTION R         298.15  +8.31451;                                  6000 N !
$ ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ Element data
$ ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ Nb
$
$ CBCC_A12 and CUB_A13 from 06Slu not included in unary
$
 PAR  G(BCC_A2,NB),,                 +GHSERNB;,,                   N 91Din !
 PAR  G(LIQUID,NB),,                    +GLIQNB;,,                    N 91Din !
$
 FUNCTION GHSERNB   298.15  -8519.353+142.045475*T-26.4711*T*LN(T)
       +2.03475E-04*T**2-3.5012E-07*T**3+93399*T**(-1);
      2750.00  Y  -37669.3+271.720843*T-41.77*T*LN(T)+1.528238E+32*T**(-9);
      6000.00  N !
 FUNCTION GLIQNB    298.15  +29781.555-10.816418*T+GHSERNB-3.06098E-23*T**7;
      2750.00  Y  -7499.398+260.756148*T-41.77*T*LN(T);
      6000.00  N !
$ ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ Ti
$
$ BCT_A5 added in unary 3.0
$
 PAR  G(BCC_A2,TI),,                 +GBCCTI;                 4000 N 91Din !
 PAR  G(LIQUID,TI),,                    +GLIQTI;                 4000 N 91Din !
$
 FUNCTION GHSERTI   298.15  -8059.921+133.615208*T-23.9933*T*LN(T)
       -0.004777975*T**2+1.06716E-07*T**3+72636*T**(-1);
       900.00  Y  -7811.815+132.988068*T-23.9887*T*LN(T)
       -0.0042033*T**2-9.0876E-08*T**3+42680*T**(-1);
      1155.00  Y  +908.837+66.976538*T-14.9466*T*LN(T)
       -0.0081465*T**2+2.02715E-07*T**3-1477660*T**(-1);
      1941.00  Y  -124526.786+638.806871*T-87.2182461*T*LN(T)
       +0.008204849*T**2-3.04747E-07*T**3+36699805*T**(-1);
      4000.00  N !
 FUNCTION GBCCTI    298.15  -1272.064+134.71418*T-25.5768*T*LN(T)
       -6.63845E-04*T**2-2.78803E-07*T**3+7208*T**(-1);
      1155.00  Y  +6667.385+105.366379*T-22.3771*T*LN(T)
       +0.00121707*T**2-8.4534E-07*T**3-2002750*T**(-1);
      1941.00  Y  +26483.26-182.426471*T+19.0900905*T*LN(T)
       -0.02200832*T**2+1.228863E-06*T**3+1400501*T**(-1);
      4000.00  N !
 FUNCTION GLIQTI    298.15  +12194.415-6.980938*T+GHSERTI;
      1300.00  Y  +369519.198-2554.0225*T+342.059267*T*LN(T)
       -0.163409355*T**2+1.2457117E-05*T**3-67034516*T**(-1);
      1941.00  Y  -19887.066+298.7367*T-46.29*T*LN(T);
      4000.00  N !
 FUNCTION GFCCTI    298.15  +GHSERTI+6000-0.1*T;                       4000 N !
$ ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ Binary systems
$ ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ Nb-Ti
$
$ From Y. Zhang et al. 2001 (Included in LB Vol. 4)
$
$ Y. Zhang, H. Liu, Z. Jin, Calphad, 25, 305-17(2001).
$
$ Checked against LB. Checked at 6000K.
$
$ Original dataset includes the metastable (at normal pressure) omega phase.
$
 PAR  L(LIQUID,NB,TI;0),,               +7406.1;,,                    N 01Zha !
$
 PAR  L(BCC_A2,NB,TI;0),,            +13045.3;,,                   N 01Zha !
$

$ Phase field specific parameters

$ Latent heat, J/cm^3 (could get this from pycalphad, but easier to just input for now!)
FUNCTION NB_L 0 2435; 6000 N !
FUNCTION TI_L 0 1755; 6000 N !

$ Melting Point, K (could also get this from pycalphad)
FUNCTION NB_TM 0 2750; 6000 N !
FUNCTION TI_TM 0 1941; 6000 N !

$ Surface energy, J/cm^2
FUNCTION NB_S 0 0.0000190334; 6000 N !
FUNCTION TI_S 0 0.0000135492; 6000 N !

$ Linear kinetic coefficient, cm/(K*s)
FUNCTION NB_B 0 0.4; 6000 N !
FUNCTION TI_B 0 0.4; 6000 N !

$ Molar Volume, cm^3/mol
FUNCTION V_M 0 12.3479824568; 6000 N !

$ Diffusion of solute, cm^2/s
FUNCTION D_L 0 0.00001; 6000 N !
FUNCTION D_S 0 0.000000001; 6000 N !

$ Orientational Mobility, 1/(s*J)
FUNCTION M_Q 0 400000000; 6000 N !

$ Orientational energy, J/(K*cm)
FUNCTION H 0 0.00000000001; 6000 N !

$ Anisotropy
FUNCTION Y_E 0 0.03; 6000 N !

